    "hypothesis": "A hybrid that uses contiguous row-major rolling DP only for obstacle-dense small grids, and sparse coordinate-sorted inclusion-exclusion otherwise, avoids allocating an N² grid for large sparse instances and improves cache locality in the dense path.",
    "notes": "The sparse path deduplicates obstacles, handles blocked endpoints, and uses O(N + B) storage; the dense fallback is bounded to N <= 4096.",
